   215	
   216	**Lambda Functions.** A lambda function is an anonymous function that can be defined on the fly in the code (as in Listing 1). It
   217	can accept any number of arguments, though it is constrained to
   218	contain only a single expression. A lambda expression in Python is
   219	defined as:
   220	**lambda** arguments **:** expression.
   221	**List Comprehensions.** A list comprehension iterates over a list
   222	of objects, checks for a specified condition (if any), and computes an
   223	expression. This computed value becomes an element in the newly
   224	created collection (as shown in Listing 2). A list comprehension can
   225	be defined with the following syntax:
   226	
   227	[expression **for** item **in** iterable **if** condition]
   228	**Map/Reduce/Filter Functions.** Map(), reduce() and filter(),
   229	are three high-order Python functions. They take a function as a
   230	parameter and return a function. They have a similar syntax:
   231	FUN (function, iterable)
   232	
   233	
   234	
   235	where FUN is either map, filter, or reduce.
   236	map() applies a given function to all items in an iterable ( _e.g.,_
   237	a list) and returns an iterator storing the obtained values (as in
   238	Listing 3 where it returns the square of each element).
   239	reduce() systematically applies a function (requiring two arguments) to the items within an iterable, progressively producing a
   240	singular value. The initial application is carried out on the first two
   241	elements of the iterable, followed by applications involving the partial result and the subsequent element. As shown in Listing 3, the
   242	reduce() function calculates the product of the values contained
   243	in the numbers iterable.
   244	
   245	filter() applies a given function to each element of the iterable,
   246	producing a Boolean result, keeping only the elements for which
   247	the return value is True . As an example, in the Listing 4, the filter
   248	function retains only the even numbers from the list.
